intuition:
Think of a skateboarder gliding along a curved ramp. At the exact instant they pass one specific spot, if you freeze time, the direction they are moving in traces out a straight line that just grazes the ramp at that single point without crossing into it — nowhere else on the ramp does the line touch again. That straight line is the tangent line (접선) to the curve at that point, and its steepness is nothing other than the curve's instantaneous rate of change there.

{{graph:tangent-intuition-parabola}}

💡 The tangent line's slope (기울기) equals the derivative (도함수) evaluated at that exact point, so finding a tangent line is really just point-slope form with $m = f'(x_0)$.
